  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")",
 StyleBox["\.b9",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " coefficient; at order p",
 StyleBox["\:2074",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", 3 q",
 StyleBox["\:2074",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/(d(d+2))."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4405bee-4993-42cd-aef6-1fd82315a102"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: A direction average instead of a \
Laplacian",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "The usual trick takes (",
 StyleBox["\[Del]\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_p)",
 StyleBox["\:207f",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " at p = 0 and divides by its value on (p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")",
 StyleBox["\:207f",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ". It needs explicit vectors or a hand-coded Laplacian on ",
 StyleBox["scal",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " expressions, and the previous version of the library got it right only for \
n ",
 StyleBox["\[LessEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 1. The direction average works with ",
 StyleBox["scal[p, p]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["scal[p, q]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " as two scalars, any n, with one table of ",
 StyleBox["\:27e8",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "c^{2k}",
 StyleBox["\:27e9",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ". The old operator is kept as a test-only reference (",
 StyleBox["tests/reference/OldProjection.wl",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "), and the new one is required to agree with it on every existing integrand \
(",
 StyleBox["design/MOMENTUMPROJECTION.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"3f7316b1-c2ee-4a67-91ac-f6d44566814a"],

Cell["4. Derivatives of \[CapitalDelta]", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6b3763f5-b1da-4bb9-8237-c568cc06e07d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Differentiating ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta][nu + wL, s]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " with respect to ",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " produces the derivative of the inert function ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04c6443e-fe40-4c18-8882-ef53da85aa0e"],

Cell["D[\[CapitalDelta][nu + w, s], nu]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dba72eff-88a3-4f2e-b27c-025739697b6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: Derivative of several arguments",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Derivative[i, j][f][x, y]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]\:2071",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_x ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]\:02b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_y f; a pattern ",
 StyleBox["Derivative[i_, j_][\[CapitalDelta]][w_, s_]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " matches any such derivative.",
 "\n\n",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " has no definition, so ",
 StyleBox["D",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " writes its derivatives with ",
 StyleBox["Derivative",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["D and unknown functions",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 04)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 "). ",
 StyleBox["deltaCompletion",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is a rule that replaces any derivative of ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " by the derivative of its polynomial form ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalSigma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_m c_m(s) (i",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")^m, so derivatives come out in the atoms ",
 StyleBox["DeltaCoefficient[m][s]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and their s-derivatives."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"2758cb1c-e618-4eb0-99a9-1d9e0f6dbb9e"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:17-19 *)
(* derivatives of Delta(w, s) = sum_m c_m(s) (I w)^m *)
deltaCompletion[deg_] := Derivative[i_, j_][\\[CapitalDelta]][w_, s_] :>
   (D[Sum[DeltaCoefficient[mm][xs] (I yw)^mm, {mm, 0, deg}], {yw, i}, {xs, \
j}] /. {yw -> w, xs -> s});\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"eb0a0ba5-88c5-4927-bc26-edb15b544bb1"],

Cell["\<\
D[\[CapitalDelta][nu + w, s], nu] /. FRGscalarMSR`Private`deltaCompletion[1]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f5b4f298-9490-4167-b35c-c6d7f5889306"],

Cell["5. Building the integrands, and the checks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"46762ae7-5cc2-466d-a158-6e520626f0d4"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:92-123 *)
ProjectOnMonomials[loops_, symmetries_] := Block[{$FRGModule = \"Projection\"},
  Module[{t0 = AbsoluteTime[], v, prop, dim, deg, targets, lhsBad, byPair, \
res, nmax, nExplicit, checks = {}, warns = {}, stage, wq, eps},
   validateStage[loops, \"Loops\"]; validateStage[symmetries, \
\"Symmetries\"];
   v = loops[\"Vertices\"]; prop = loops[\"Propagator\"];
   FRGAssert[\"Projection.sameAnsatz\", v[\"Upstream\"] === \
symmetries[\"Upstream\"], {v[\"Upstream\"], symmetries[\"Upstream\"]},
    \"the loops and the symmetries were built from different ansatz \
stages\"];
   dim = symmetries[\"Dimension\"]; deg = prop[\"DeltaDegree\"]; wq = \
LoopVariables[loops];
   eps = Lookup[v[\"Ansatz\"], \"Epsilon\", False];
   If[eps, AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Projection.epsilonDimension\", dim \
=== 2, dim, \"internal: eps (jac) needs the declared d = 2\", \"eps with d = \
2\"]]];
   $wedgeDropped = 0;
   targets = Select[symmetries[\"Classification\"], #Class =!= \"Structure\" \
&];
   nmax = Max[0, targets[[All, \"Momentum\"]]];

   (* the d-normalisation of the momentum projection, against an independent \
closed form (LHS cannot see it: review E2) *)
   If[nmax >= 1, checkNormalisation[nmax, dim];
    AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Projection.normalisation\", True, Null, \"\
\",
      \"(p.q)^(2k) (p^2)^(n-k) -> <c^(2k)> q^(2k) = q^(2k) Gamma(k+1/2) \
Gamma(d/2)/(Sqrt[Pi] Gamma(k+d/2)), n <= \" <> ToString[nmax] <> \", d = \" \
<> ToString[dim]]]];
   If[nmax >= 2, AppendTo[warns, infoCheck[\"ASSUMPTION\", \
\"Projection.shapeSmoothness\",
      \"p^{2n} flows contain shape derivatives up to order 2n (here \" <> \
ToString[2 nmax] <> \"): any explicit shape substituted later must be C^\" <> \
ToString[2 nmax]]]];

   (* LHS check: the projection operator applied to Gamma_k (regulator off) \
reproduces the classified coefficient *)
   lhsBad = Select[targets, Expand[project[VertexValue[v, #Pair, {{nu, p}}], \
#Frequency, #Momentum, {nu, p}, {zz, zq}, dim, deg, eps] - #GammaK] =!= 0 &];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Projection.LHS\", lhsBad === {}, lhsBad,
     \"internal: the projection operator does not reproduce the Gamma_k \
coefficient (normalisation of the frequency or momentum projection)\",
     \"projection of Gamma_k = its coefficient, \" <> \
ToString[Length[targets]] <> \" monomials ((d/d(I nu))^m/m!, (p^2)^n \
coefficient; not the d-normalisation)\"]];

   byPair = GroupBy[targets, #Pair &];
   res = Join @@ KeyValueMap[Function[{pair, ms}, Module[{loop = \
LoopIntegrand[loops, pair, nu, p]},
        Function[r, With[{ig = project[loop, r[\"Frequency\"], \
r[\"Momentum\"], {nu, p}, wq, dim, deg, eps]},
           (* n >= 2: the directional average against explicit vectors (n <= \
1 is certified by the regression vs the old operator) *)
           If[r[\"Momentum\"] >= 2, checkExplicitVectors[loop, ig, \
r[\"Frequency\"], r[\"Momentum\"], {nu, p}, wq, dim, deg]];
           Append[r, \"Integrand\" -> ig]]] /@ ms]], byPair];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"4054e266-5bbf-41af-b741-610cb3fa0a07"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The integrands are computed per pair: ",
 StyleBox["GroupBy[targets, #Pair &]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["GroupBy and KeyValueMap",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 02)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 ") groups the monomials, and ",
 StyleBox["LoopIntegrand",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (lesson 07) is called once per pair, then projected once per monomial."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"559ee080-04c4-43e6-b0b4-fc1cc4a2b7e7"],

Cell["\<\
Three checks guard the operator, each independent of the others:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b015b4a5-d0ad-4219-be25-c12b0e9b3e27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["`Projection.LHS`",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": the same ",
 StyleBox["project",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", applied to ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_k itself (regulator off), must give back each classified coefficient. It \
tests the frequency normalisation and the order in s; ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_k depends on p only through p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", so it cannot see the d-normalisation (review E2)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"aef70371-696b-4b27-b263-57ba10465bed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["`Projection.normalisation`",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": the projection of (p",
 StyleBox["\[CenterDot]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "q)^{2k} (p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")^{n",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "k} against the closed form q^{2k} ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(k+",
 StyleBox["\.bd",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(d/2)/(",
 StyleBox["\[Sqrt]\[Pi]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(k+d/2)), written with ",
 StyleBox["Gamma",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " instead of ",
 StyleBox["projCAverage",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (review E17)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0d637f9b-7705-4d76-a464-fbbde5b5fa62"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["`Projection.explicitVectors`",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", for n ",
 StyleBox["\[GreaterEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 2: the result against (",
 StyleBox["\[Del]\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_p)",
 StyleBox["\:207f",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/N_n computed on explicit d-component vectors, at the declared d, or at d = \
1, ",
 StyleBox["\[Ellipsis]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", n+1 for a symbolic d."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e2eb9a12-e83a-4cee-94d4-d9f0a7157003"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:34-35 *)
(* N_n = (Laplacian_p)^n (p^2)^n = 4^n n! (d/2)_n  (M2) *)
lapNorm[n_, d_] := 4^n n! Pochhammer[d/2, n];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"2a6c248f-acbf-43a9-bb0d-27a32589694b"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:37-44 *)
(* the same projection on explicit d-vectors: (Laplacian_p)^n at p = 0 / N_n; \
returns {coefficient, q.q}. Independent of
   directionalAverage and projCAverage (used by Projection.explicitVectors \
and the tests) *)
explicitProjection[e0_, m_, n_, {nu_, p_}, {w_, q_}, d_Integer, deg_] := \
Module[{pc = Array[projPc, d], qc = Array[projQc, d], vec, e},
   vec = {p -> pc, q -> qc};
   e = e0 /. {scal[a_, b_] :> Expand[(a /. vec) . (b /. vec)], wedge[a_, b_] \
:> With[{x = a /. vec, y = b /. vec}, x[[1]] y[[2]] - x[[2]] y[[1]]]};
   If[m > 0, e = D[e, {nu, m}]];
   e = Nest[Function[g, Sum[D[g, {x, 2}], {x, pc}]], e, n] /. Thread[pc -> 0] \
/. nu -> 0;
   {(e /. deltaCompletion[deg])/(I^m m! lapNorm[n, d]), qc . qc}];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"8c8429ae-808e-4b02-84f7-dab3c1c39ba5"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:54-61 *)
(* Projection.normalisation: the full projection of (p.q)^(2k) (p^2)^(n-k) \
against <c^(2k)> q^(2k) = q^(2k) Gamma(k+1/2) Gamma(d/2) /
   (Sqrt[Pi] Gamma(k+d/2)), written independently of projCAverage (review \
E17) *)
checkNormalisation[nmax_, dim_] := Module[{bad},
   bad = Select[Flatten[Table[{n, k}, {n, 1, nmax}, {k, 0, n}], 1], \
Function[nk, With[{n = nk[[1]], k = nk[[2]]},
        Together[FunctionExpand[project[scal[nP, nQ]^(2 k) scal[nP, nP]^(n - \
k), 0, n, {nNu, nP}, {nW, nQ}, dim, 0] -
            LoopMomentumSquared^k Gamma[k + 1/2] Gamma[dim/2]/(Sqrt[Pi] \
Gamma[k + dim/2])]] =!= 0]]];
   FRGAssert[\"Projection.normalisation\", bad === {}, bad,
    \"internal: the projection of (p.q)^(2k) (p^2)^(n-k) differs from \
<c^(2k)> q^(2k) (these {n, k})\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"7462321d-e2b2-4ee8-bb4e-66ffbd8878b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: Nest",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Nest[f, x, n]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " applies f to x n times: ",
 StyleBox["f[f[f[x]]]",
