}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25202f00-2e4e-482d-a471-c353b54f59d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: Why the explicit check is needed only for \
n \[GreaterEqual] 2, at n+1 dimensions",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "A p^{2n} projection is a rational function of d whose numerator can be \
written with n+1 independent d-structures, so agreeing at n+1 integer \
dimensions pins it down for every d (review E4). For n ",
 StyleBox["\[LessEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 1 the regression against the old operator certifies the result already, \
and the KPZ example of these lessons has n ",
 StyleBox["\[LessEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 1, so its card has no ",
 StyleBox["explicitVectors",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " line. The p",
 StyleBox["\:2074",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " flows are tested against the literature in ",
 StyleBox["benchmarks/KuramotoSivashinsky",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"6ef5af28-09c4-48b4-ae35-868f6862bb2b"],

Cell["6. With \[CurlyEpsilon] (d = 2)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"00c8c3b8-63e7-4c29-8719-cd099c457493"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:63-80 *)
(* with eps (d = 2): products of wedges are reduced by F2; every term is then \
wedge[p, q]^e f(p^2, p.q, q^2, nu) with e = 0 or 1, and
   the e = 1 part has a vanishing (I nu)^m (p^2)^n projection for every n \
(M3; F4 of design/LEVICIVITA.md): it is dropped, after
   checking that its projection vanishes on explicit 2-vectors. $wedgeDropped \
counts the integrands with a nonzero dropped part. *)
dropWedge[e0_, m_, n_, {nu_, p_}, {w_, q_}] := Module[{e = \
FRGscalarMSR`Internal`reduceWedge2D[e0], ew, odd, ex, pc, qc, vec},
   ew = e /. {wedge[p, q] -> wz, wedge[q, p] -> -wz};
   FRGAssert[\"Projection.wedgeOdd\", FreeQ[ew, wedge] && Exponent[ew, wz] <= \
1 && FreeQ[ew, Power[wz, _?Negative]],
    Cases[ew, _wedge | Power[wz, _], {0, Infinity}], \"internal: a wedge \
other than +-wedge[p, q] to the power <= 1 is left after the 2D reduction\"];
   odd = Coefficient[ew, wz, 1];
   If[odd =!= 0,
    vec = {p -> {pc[1], pc[2]}, q -> {qc[1], qc[2]}};
    ex = (pc[1] qc[2] - pc[2] qc[1]) odd /. scal[a_, b_] :> Expand[(a /. vec) \
. (b /. vec)];
    If[m > 0, ex = D[ex, {nu, m}]];
    ex = Nest[D[#, {pc[1], 2}] + D[#, {pc[2], 2}] &, ex, n];
    ex = ex /. {pc[_] -> 0, nu -> 0};
    FRGAssert[\"Projection.wedgeOdd\", ExactlyZeroQ[ex, \"Seeds\" -> {1}], \
Short[ex],
     \"internal: the part odd in wedge[p, q] has a nonzero projection \
(explicit 2-vectors)\"];
    $wedgeDropped++];
   ew /. wz -> 0];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"6bd9f879-229a-4743-9e94-3d6da25fa96f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 StyleBox["jac",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", products of wedges are first reduced to scalar products (",
 StyleBox["reduceWedge2D",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", lesson 00, section 7). Every term is then wedge[p, q]^e f(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", p",
 StyleBox["\[CenterDot]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "q, q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") with e = 0 or 1, and the e = 1 part has a vanishing projection for every \
m and n: reflecting e about q keeps c and flips the sign of wedge[e, q] (M3, ",
 StyleBox["design/LEVICIVITA.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " F4). It is dropped, after checking on explicit 2-vectors that its \
projection really vanishes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"87f9587a-0024-4f36-916d-21583f22fba1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["$wedgeDropped",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is one of the few global variables of the library: a private counter, \
reset by ",
 StyleBox["ProjectOnMonomials",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and read for its card line. ",
 StyleBox["$wedgeDropped++",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " adds 1 to it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2524f7c7-7f9f-48cf-8124-0f203e09d96f"],

Cell["7. The stage", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"81a0bba6-cb38-466e-9b5e-d41a2c3f7c47"],

